<% content_for :stylesheets, area_stylesheet_link_tags("simulator") %>

<header class="page-hero page-hero--home">
  <div>
    <h1>Nearby traffic, in your pocket.</h1>
    <p class="page-hero-subtitle">skyBlip Go transmits your position in ADS&#8209;L and shows ADS&#8209;L and FLARM traffic. skyBlip Bravo detects Mode S and ADS&#8209;B transponders. Together they make skyBlip Tango.</p>
  </div>
  <figure class="hero-figure">
    <%= content_image_tag "pages/index/skyblip-go-techo.avif", alt: "" %>
  </figure>
</header>

<section id="journey" class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">From the first try to your first flight</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">Whether you fly a light aircraft, a microlight, a glider or a paraglider, we&rsquo;ll guide you at each step.</p>
  <div class="journey">
    <ol class="journey-steps">
      <li>
        <h3><%= link_to_page "skyblip-go", label: "Try it" %></h3>
        <p>Try the radar in the simulator.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><%= link_to_page "buy", label: "Get one" %></h3>
        <p>An off-the-shelf device. The software is free.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><%= link_to_page "install", label: "Install it" %></h3>
        <p>From your browser, with Briefing.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="journey-end"><strong>You&rsquo;re ready to fly.</strong> The <%= link_to_page "guides", label: "first steps guide" %> shows you the essentials.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="where-to-look" class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">See and be seen, <span class="highlight">with a Go</span></h2>

  <div class="feature">
    <div>
      <h3>A radar <span class="highlight">you can read at a glance</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        You are in the centre, track up. Each traffic icon shows whether the aircraft
        is above, level with you or below. Its line shows where it will be in a minute.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "radar.png", alt: "The radar page: three aircraft, one above, one below, one level and climbing, each with a line showing where it will be in a minute" %>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="feature feature--reverse">
    <div>
      <h3>An alarm <span class="highlight">that gives the direction</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        Within 3&nbsp;km and 300&nbsp;m, a quarter of the screen flashes on the
        side of the traffic.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "alarm.png", alt: "The radar page during an alarm: the quarter of the screen facing the traffic has turned black" %>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="feature">
    <div>
      <h3>Your position <span class="highlight">broadcast every second</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        In flight, the Go broadcasts your position in ADS-L every second. Any
        aircraft fitted with ADS-L sees you and your callsign.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "nearby.png", alt: "The Nearby page: five aircraft, those at your height first, with their source ADS-L or FLARM, their callsign, their distance and their height above or below you" %>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="feature feature--reverse">
    <div>
      <h3>The traffic <span class="highlight">in your app</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        Over Bluetooth, the traffic shows up in SDVFR Next, SkyDemon,
        ForeFlight and other apps.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot shot--photo shot--app">
      <%= pages_image_tag "sdvfr-next-traffic.avif", alt: "SDVFR Next: the map with the traffic received from skyBlip Go, each aircraft labelled with its callsign" %>
      <figcaption>SkyDreamSoft SDVFR Next <a href="https://skydreamsoft.fr">skydreamsoft.fr</a></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <p class="signature"><%= link_to_page "features", label: "See every feature" %></p>
</section>

<section id="simulator" class="band band--tint try-radar">
  <h2 class="section-title">Try the radar</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">Find an aircraft. Its shape tells you whether it&rsquo;s above, at your level or below. Follow its track line.</p>
  <%= render "shared/simulator_loader", loading: :lazy %>
  <p class="try-radar-bravo">Tick &quot;With Bravo (skyBlip Tango)&quot; to restart the simulator and see aircraft fitted with ADS-B farther away.</p>
  <p class="try-radar-more"><%= link_to_page "skyblip-go", label: "Open the full simulator", class: "button button--primary" %></p>
</section>

<section id="devices" class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">Which device is right for you?</h2>
  <figure class="pair">
    <%= content_image_tag "pages/index/skyblip-go-techo.avif", alt: "skyBlip Go, a white device with an antenna and traffic radar on its e-paper screen." %>
    <span class="pair-plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
    <%= content_image_tag "pages/skyblip-bravo/seeed-x1.avif", alt: "skyBlip Bravo, a black Seeed SenseCAP MeshTracker X1 about the size of a card.", class: "photo-x1" %>
  </figure>
  <ul>
    <li><%= link_to_page "features", label: "Go" %> transmits your position in ADS-L and shows ADS-L and FLARM traffic. Go shows gliders equipped with FLARM, but it doesn&rsquo;t transmit FLARM or replace your FLARM.</li>
    <li><%= link_to_page "skyblip-bravo", label: "Bravo" %> detects Mode S and ADS-B transponders and sends ADS-B traffic to your navigation app. It doesn&rsquo;t transmit your position.</li>
    <li><%= link_to_page "skyblip-tango", label: "Tango" %> pairs a Go with a Bravo. See all three types of traffic on Go&rsquo;s radar while Go keeps transmitting your position in ADS-L.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="value" class="band band--blip">
  <h2 class="section-title">Off-the-shelf hardware, from €68</h2>
  <p>Buy a LilyGO T-Echo for Go or a MeshTracker X1 for Bravo. You pay for the hardware. The software and updates are free, with no subscription. The code is open source. Anyone can read and check it.</p>
  <div class="quote">
    <blockquote>
      &quot;Safety isn&rsquo;t a premium feature. Our safety features for recreational flying and air sports stay open source and free.&quot;
    </blockquote>
  </div>
  <p class="signature"><%= link_to_page "buy", label: "See the hardware and prices", class: "button button--primary" %> · <%= link_to_page "about", label: "Read our pledge" %></p>
</section>

<section id="questions" class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">What pilots ask before buying</h2>
  <div class="faq">
    <details>
      <summary>Who can see me?</summary>
      <p>Pilots with equipment that can receive your ADS-L signal can see the position your Go transmits. Go receives FLARM but doesn&rsquo;t transmit it. Bravo doesn&rsquo;t transmit your position.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I see aircraft with transponders?</summary>
      <p>Yes for aircraft equipped with ADS-B. With Bravo, their positions appear in your navigation app or on a paired Go. Mode S alone gives no position. Bravo detects it, and we&rsquo;re collecting data to work out how best to report it on Go and in navigation apps.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need a subscription?</summary>
      <p>No. You buy the hardware. Position transmissions, traffic, alerts and updates need no subscription.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Is it certified?</summary>
      <p>No. skyBlip is an uncertified aid to visual lookout. Keep looking outside. Aircraft won&rsquo;t appear unless your device receives a compatible signal. Keep the equipment required for your flight.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need a phone?</summary>
      <p>Go has its own screen. With Bravo on its own, use a compatible app on a phone or tablet to see traffic. In a Tango, Go shows it.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I go back to the original software?</summary>
      <p>Yes. skyBlip leaves the program that installs the software in place. You can download the original software of the T-Echo and the X1 from the web to reinstall it.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
